"Amazon Augmented AI":{"security":["For Amazon Augmented AI, separate model, prompt, index, dataset, endpoint and operator permissions; use least-privilege roles for training, inference and retrieval.","Encrypt training data, prompts, documents, outputs and logs, apply data residency/retention controls, and keep sensitive content out of shared telemetry.","Audit model, endpoint, knowledge-base, agent, guardrail and evaluation changes; require approval before promoting artifacts or changing access."],"optimization":["Choose Amazon Augmented AI's native inference, retrieval, batch, streaming, fine-tuning or human-review path from latency, accuracy and volume requirements.","Reduce payload and context size, reuse embeddings/caches where safe, batch offline work and select model/instance size from measured quality-per-cost.","Keep preprocessing, evaluation, monitoring and serving stages separable so each can scale and fail independently."],"cost":["Model Amazon Augmented AI using its documented token, unit, page, character, image, training, endpoint, storage or human-review dimensions.","Prompt/context length, endpoint idle time, repeated retrieval, model choice and dataset processing can dominate; measure them separately.","Include S3, OpenSearch/vector stores, CloudWatch, data transfer, orchestration and downstream application costs."],"watchPoints":["Amazon Augmented AI has a distinct quality, quota and lifecycle boundary; validate grounding, drift, model version, latency and fallback behavior in production.","Generated or extracted output still needs application authorization, validation and human escalation where the use case requires it.","Track throttling, failed invocations, token/page limits, index freshness, model/endpoint status and sensitive-data leakage."]},
